$F(x)=-4{x}^{2}-3x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ What is $f(x)$ for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,\\pi ),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,\\pi ), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-\\pi ,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-(-4(-x)^{2}-3(-x)) \\\\  & =-(-4{x}^{2}+3x) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340868/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5ee3c3f-4289-5e38-a47a-52e5c2ad3817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340868"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341406/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer/id #uuid "bb6411d5-48ed-5c97-bb32-2ae27b8e9b4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341406/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "dd7e6b2a-a5c8-5460-8f64-1a48e8e2b6e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341406/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d00205a4-0c85-5c1d-9631-4227fda4bec0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341406/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer-field/choices ["q-341406/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" "q-341406/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341406" :question/id #uuid "5e2cfe5b-fb22-538b-9922-148d7cee940d" :question/math-academy-id "q-341406" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}-2x$ for $x\\in [0,10),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-10,10).$ What is the value of $f(-6)?$\n\n$f(-6)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,10),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,10), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-10,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-10,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-((-x)^{2}-2(-x)) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-6) & =-(-6)^{2}-2(-6)=-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341406/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5ee3c3f-4289-5e38-a47a-52e5c2ad3817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341406"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341210/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "5e858c2c-77a2-5510-8d00-d70684676589" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341210/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1559f4a4-aafb-5525-b562-2afbf72d9e22" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341210/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-341210/field-1/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341210" :question/id #uuid "3dabab92-3d7b-5238-8b01-823555b737d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-341210" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=-{x}^{2}+5x$ for $x\\in [0,8),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-8,8).$ What is the value of $f(-3)?$\n\n$f(-3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,8),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,8), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-8,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-8,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-(-(-x)^{2}+5(-x)) \\\\  & =-(-{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{2}+5(-3)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341210/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5ee3c3f-4289-5e38-a47a-52e5c2ad3817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340926/field-1/ecd5d50340c3e4134134216fce6f49c9c64f119897e0df8a7a91a202fbe11117" :answer/id #uuid "a933e85c-8b10-55af-9b3c-95cdd70e9db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10(1+(-1)^{n})}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340926/field-1/929797849051ed1ce36d2698c73a6c78fa2d092aaffae1c8755fd37e9c5a198c" :answer/id #uuid "07a684a3-b675-5a55-ad98-e8e65c20cdc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340926/field-1/faf88543bceccf327f170e7f26658d90f6bd561b4e28d6c20dbbd8fc30b2de88" :answer/id #uuid "b0fccebf-a72b-5fba-9f32-a1e6461ac17e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340926/field-1/7a2f35554aa4430eb6a7cc213cbdc26fa152d31af0545f2c2bc1811f88cb5c92" :answer/id #uuid "86db0ec1-de4f-58da-a632-c3cd25b7b9a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10(1-(-1)^{n})}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340926/field-1/2a87ade02268bcc87ee560884593f43e0670bef5d39e343664b7a03a23d58cc7" :answer/id #uuid "0f507569-dcd3-5e05-b7db-7b669f249974" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5(1-(-1)^{n})}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340926/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "81ced504-7588-5c35-9864-a3d5341abf7e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340926/field-1/faf88543bceccf327f170e7f26658d90f6bd561b4e28d6c20dbbd8fc30b2de88" :answer-field/choices ["q-340926/field-1/ecd5d50340c3e4134134216fce6f49c9c64f119897e0df8a7a91a202fbe11117" "q-340926/field-1/929797849051ed1ce36d2698c73a6c78fa2d092aaffae1c8755fd37e9c5a198c" "q-340926/field-1/faf88543bceccf327f170e7f26658d90f6bd561b4e28d6c20dbbd8fc30b2de88" "q-340926/field-1/7a2f35554aa4430eb6a7cc213cbdc26fa152d31af0545f2c2bc1811f88cb5c92" "q-340926/field-1/2a87ade02268bcc87ee560884593f43e0670bef5d39e343664b7a03a23d58cc7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340926" :question/id #uuid "c587c539-44e0-5aa3-9938-b12fa29ef0b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-340926" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-5x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${b}_{n}.$\n$\\,{b}_{n}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-5x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{10}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{10}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{n\\pi }(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340926/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a85c9c4-8563-55e0-9d4f-7d61d3be6243"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340926"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-340629"] :question/problem "Let $F(x)=-5x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-5x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{10}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{10}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{n\\pi }(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{10(-1)^{n}}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-341381/field-1/6ac39e60259bdeef83c2771f348db1dac1394363878bc6e8d5a7ab7213ab9dad" :answer/id #uuid "48c85509-281d-55f3-8b3d-65a7049dbbca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(-2\\pi -3)-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341381/field-1/e56ef1d8e0e721305c399616910e469f684e99ec734c1dc763faa1f3eb9075c3" :answer/id #uuid "0e3ed4d9-7ce7-56b6-8e38-2955ce72a53d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341381/field-1/1b285d32a935f0f17cc208fda94155cf2713c66511852dcf56d56c1ea7d69ae2" :answer/id #uuid "7c43f418-2c6e-5bc2-bf4a-e8aa070f1282" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(2\\pi +3)-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341381/field-1/49ed3fbe73da3db8070d30ebc33c03b778e0ff6e9db3b8c368ef523b5cbdd660" :answer/id #uuid "2e13b837-4381-5713-bc98-972f2fef9780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(2\\pi -3)+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341381/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "76bf59f8-6ff0-5ad2-8501-a2d1951e11b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341381/field-1/49ed3fbe73da3db8070d30ebc33c03b778e0ff6e9db3b8c368ef523b5cbdd660" :answer-field/choices ["q-341381/field-1/6ac39e60259bdeef83c2771f348db1dac1394363878bc6e8d5a7ab7213ab9dad" "q-341381/field-1/e56ef1d8e0e721305c399616910e469f684e99ec734c1dc763faa1f3eb9075c3" "q-341381/field-1/1b285d32a935f0f17cc208fda94155cf2713c66511852dcf56d56c1ea7d69ae2" "q-341381/field-1/49ed3fbe73da3db8070d30ebc33c03b778e0ff6e9db3b8c368ef523b5cbdd660"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341381" :question/id #uuid "b48fb2c2-63f4-51b9-922e-bb1335d6cc70" :question/math-academy-id "q-341381" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-2x+3$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${b}_{n}.$$\\,{b}_{n}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-2x+3$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-2x+3\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[(-2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{2}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((-2\\pi +3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-3\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{2}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-2\\pi +3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-3+\\frac{2}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-2\\pi +3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-2\\pi +3)(-1)^{n}-3)=\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(2\\pi -3)+3).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341381/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a85c9c4-8563-55e0-9d4f-7d61d3be6243"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-1/663d534c15851a130874ec021a253cffad4103b1506a5961fc9149ec79e04ad8" :answer/id #uuid "34a49133-0254-5c12-8394-c5fe72bc6f0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-1/d3f0ae8812df9b87b9a7dbb17993f2aa72a870f0a2d48fa558e68cacc4bb6705" :answer/id #uuid "da8690b4-fded-5707-afde-170360bbbecd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-1/e56ef1d8e0e721305c399616910e469f684e99ec734c1dc763faa1f3eb9075c3" :answer/id #uuid "636a450b-8b5f-553f-93c2-66d91d811bfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-1/0162931aafb3f17b7096b1f04d1e5e6822c7d2e36785db317bf2ef0be896ca0d" :answer/id #uuid "f9b8eb37-1394-52ac-b48b-03d3edb8b038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3(-1)^{n}}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "79f75ea3-3c9e-55e2-a27d-9c0c36d9955d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340922/field-1/d3f0ae8812df9b87b9a7dbb17993f2aa72a870f0a2d48fa558e68cacc4bb6705" :answer-field/choices ["q-340922/field-1/663d534c15851a130874ec021a253cffad4103b1506a5961fc9149ec79e04ad8" "q-340922/field-1/d3f0ae8812df9b87b9a7dbb17993f2aa72a870f0a2d48fa558e68cacc4bb6705" "q-340922/field-1/e56ef1d8e0e721305c399616910e469f684e99ec734c1dc763faa1f3eb9075c3" "q-340922/field-1/0162931aafb3f17b7096b1f04d1e5e6822c7d2e36785db317bf2ef0be896ca0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-2/3f6a3aa25491ef321371576cb221342060d043d2422df9923d1f53fc94cde6cd" :answer/id #uuid "0eee691b-9734-5389-ae43-e5155c56b35d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-2/454707892878cf2dd9571a67e15af8dfb75023edf431627663fe6dd748702707" :answer/id #uuid "ddbe744d-84ff-5f61-a7c5-7802927e40c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-2/3a86edc502d0038df0dcd390c378431e5286836bbdd60033424dd2f8510c1df7" :answer/id #uuid "11d339cd-fd6e-5b04-b877-5e266abbcd65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-2/fd0623bef64bcb0a0ce9b59f822de4999c714270edbdc40bbf7ea19c5354d539" :answer/id #uuid "0b76ea7a-b6ef-5b09-b4a3-bbbbf072acff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5f12986-7678-53c9-af61-db9b8910865f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340922/field-2/3a86edc502d0038df0dcd390c378431e5286836bbdd60033424dd2f8510c1df7" :answer-field/choices ["q-340922/field-2/3f6a3aa25491ef321371576cb221342060d043d2422df9923d1f53fc94cde6cd" "q-340922/field-2/454707892878cf2dd9571a67e15af8dfb75023edf431627663fe6dd748702707" "q-340922/field-2/3a86edc502d0038df0dcd390c378431e5286836bbdd60033424dd2f8510c1df7" "q-340922/field-2/fd0623bef64bcb0a0ce9b59f822de4999c714270edbdc40bbf7ea19c5354d539"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340922" :question/id #uuid "c34511e4-c391-5078-b8b3-a04fa93212e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-340922" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=-3x$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-3x$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{6}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{6}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{n\\pi }(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6(-1)^{n}}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340922/field-1" "q-340922/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a85c9c4-8563-55e0-9d4f-7d61d3be6243"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340922"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-1/fccf7c1246bb5d7a652e2f68c501c7ce6abef9f0314e623a8d5518fc1f20c573" :answer/id #uuid "10b36acd-bb3f-5765-a43d-00bec04ac1e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-1/82b143fbbabe576852caea2e9d9e95d068017fe14283d7180c995dcbeefaadf3" :answer/id #uuid "fbca60e1-82d8-5f36-9fdb-a79e86858a1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi +2)-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-1/663d534c15851a130874ec021a253cffad4103b1506a5961fc9149ec79e04ad8" :answer/id #uuid "dbd20428-c3b6-5340-b88c-fed465f2a5e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3(1-(-1)^{n})}{\\pi n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-1/5e00925a1cbb6ef7f4a1593d43af447bc42e29dc3228644b6cca172955609347" :answer/id #uuid "fb921b37-0af7-5e45-a3df-c7e7204be2c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "752bd285-eed0-5fdb-9626-ab2ae238e1de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341336/field-1/5e00925a1cbb6ef7f4a1593d43af447bc42e29dc3228644b6cca172955609347" :answer-field/choices ["q-341336/field-1/fccf7c1246bb5d7a652e2f68c501c7ce6abef9f0314e623a8d5518fc1f20c573" "q-341336/field-1/82b143fbbabe576852caea2e9d9e95d068017fe14283d7180c995dcbeefaadf3" "q-341336/field-1/663d534c15851a130874ec021a253cffad4103b1506a5961fc9149ec79e04ad8" "q-341336/field-1/5e00925a1cbb6ef7f4a1593d43af447bc42e29dc3228644b6cca172955609347"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-2/3a86edc502d0038df0dcd390c378431e5286836bbdd60033424dd2f8510c1df7" :answer/id #uuid "b20a4e58-f33e-5925-80da-eac282e3fb6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-2/454707892878cf2dd9571a67e15af8dfb75023edf431627663fe6dd748702707" :answer/id #uuid "c7edcaa2-7e37-50c6-8744-a492daaeed57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-2/3f6a3aa25491ef321371576cb221342060d043d2422df9923d1f53fc94cde6cd" :answer/id #uuid "5c02e1b9-8a1e-5780-98b9-5d9001e3fe03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-2/fd0623bef64bcb0a0ce9b59f822de4999c714270edbdc40bbf7ea19c5354d539" :answer/id #uuid "ac8520f7-7e62-5614-9537-10496331115a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c47802f0-aa1d-5211-a840-15de060de3a2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341336/field-2/3a86edc502d0038df0dcd390c378431e5286836bbdd60033424dd2f8510c1df7" :answer-field/choices ["q-341336/field-2/3a86edc502d0038df0dcd390c378431e5286836bbdd60033424dd2f8510c1df7" "q-341336/field-2/454707892878cf2dd9571a67e15af8dfb75023edf431627663fe6dd748702707" "q-341336/field-2/3f6a3aa25491ef321371576cb221342060d043d2422df9923d1f53fc94cde6cd" "q-341336/field-2/fd0623bef64bcb0a0ce9b59f822de4999c714270edbdc40bbf7ea19c5354d539"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341336" :question/id #uuid "f67b8637-4bf3-58b7-8d0d-483388efc50e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341336" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=-3x+2$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ Select the correct missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-3x+2$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-3x+2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=-3x+2\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=-3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[(-3x+2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{3}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{3}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2+\\frac{3}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-3\\pi +2)(-1)^{n}-2)=\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2).\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{n\\pi }((-1)^{n}(3\\pi -2)+2)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341336/field-1" "q-341336/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a85c9c4-8563-55e0-9d4f-7d61d3be6243"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341336"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21809"] :question/problem "Let $F(x)=x^2+10x$ for $x\\in[0,6),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x \\in (-6,6).$ What is the value of $f(-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in[0,6),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/assets/3d7a4a25652434612765ebef26c7c0956342611968008bc4908a4865297e047d.png)\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in(-6,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-((-x)^{2}+10(-x)) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-10x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =-(-1)^{2}+10(-1)=-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21810"] :question/problem "Let $F(x)=4x$ for $x\\in[0,\\pi).$ Find the missing parts in the Fourier sine series of the **odd** $2\\pi$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function $F(x)$ below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068497/assets/20ec903a94cb720f0d2c50b427409e36705af1f9f226b5c6fb11f93f92f0dd49.png)" :question/worked-solution "For our Fourier sine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\nb_n=\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi f(x)\\sin(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=4x$ for $x \\in (0,\\pi).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nb_n = \\dfrac{8}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi x \\sin(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=-\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{n}[x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{n\\pi }((\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{n}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{n\\pi }(\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\frac{1}{n}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )}{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\cos(n\\pi)=(-1)^n,$ we have\n\n$$\nb_n = -\\dfrac{8(-1)^n}{n}=\\dfrac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier sine series is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\dfrac{8(-1)^{n+1}}{n} \\cdot \\sin(nx).\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
